WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.533
Tonight.

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.235
We have an extremely difficult,

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.304
important and highly compelling

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.672
conversation

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.408
in hugely unusual circumstances.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.143
Siamak Namazi, is

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.211
an Iranian-American

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.045
businessman

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.848
imprisoned in Iran for over seven years.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.683
He spoke to me over the phone

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.319
from inside the notorious Evin Prison

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.920
giving us a firsthand

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.589
look at the desperation

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.591
of foreign nationals, dual citizens

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.926
detained in that country.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.495
I first interviewed Siamak

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.230
back in the early 2000.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.965
During the reform era,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.366
a very different Iran.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.702
Then he was a prominent businessman

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.836
and an analyst

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.938
trying to build relations between Iran

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:39.739
and the West.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.141
Siamak was arrested

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:44.411
during a 2015 business trip and convicted

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:45.578
of cooperating

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.480
with a hostile foreign government.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.716
Only that government is the United States

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.118
and he is a US citizen.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.886
It's a conviction,

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.988
of course, that he completely refutes.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.823
In the following years,

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.324
American detainees

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.225
have been released

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.827
as part of prisoner swaps

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:02.195
with the United States

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.930
SEAL Marks own father

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.433
who was also arrested in 2016

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.501
while trying to visit him in prison.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.303
Was released on medical grounds

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:11.671
last October.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.640
But Siamak continues

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.874
to languish in prison,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.243
even going on a week like a week

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.211
long hunger strike.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.546
Back in January

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.815
and writing a letter to President Biden.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.551
Now he says he feels so alone,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.652
so abandoned

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.420
and so out of options

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.489
that he has decided to come to us,

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.925
hoping to beseech Biden to help him

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.527
and the other Iranian-Americans.

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.396
And here is our extraordinary

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.530
phone conversation

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.601
Siamak Namazi.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.870
It's a rare, rare thing

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.540
to hear from somebody inside Evin Prison.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.676
Can I start by asking you

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.977
to state your name

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.312
and where you are actually

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.647
talking to us from above?

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.683
My name is still Acne Rosy

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.953
and this call is being made from Ward

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:02.322
four of Evin Prison in Tehran.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.958
Siamak It's a long, long time

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.393
since we last spoke when we met in Iran.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.796
And I want to say that this is very,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.598
very unusual

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.400
to speak to somebody inside Evin Prison.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.337
Why are you speaking to us in this way?

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.840
Why are you speaking out now?

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.342
Well, Christiane, first,

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.943
it's good to hear your voice as well.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.745
After so many years

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.780
directly and not

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.582
not on the recording that someone's

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.450
playing back for me.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:32.752
I think

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.153
the very

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:33.620
fact that

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.120
I've chosen

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.388
to take this risk

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:36.322
and appearances

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.725
and from from Evin Prison,

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.160
it should just tell you

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.662
how dire my situation has become.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.430
By this point,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.533
I've been a hostage for

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.134
seven and a half years.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.737
Now I've

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.006
that's six times

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:55.341
this duration of the hostage crisis.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.677
I keep getting told

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.113
that I'm going to be rescued

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:00.813
and deals

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.183
fall apart or I get left abandoned.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:06.152
I don't honestly.

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.620
The other hostages

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.023
and I desperately need President Biden

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.692
to finally hear us out,

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.460
to finally hear our cry for help

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.862
bring us home.

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.764
And I suppose

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:18.631
desperate times

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.500
call for desperate measures.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.235
So this is a desperate measure.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:25.238
I have I'm clearly nervous,

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.874
just like it's hard for you.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.109
It's it's very intimidating for

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:30.810
me to do this.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.414
I feel I need to be heard.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:38.218
I don't know how long I have to wait

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.285
until

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.054
the White House understands

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.489
that we need action

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.625
and not just to be told

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:48.661
that bringing us out is a priority.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:50.630
Siamak, let me follow up on that,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.031
because you did write

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.333
an Op-Ed

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:54.100
that was published

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.202
in The New York Times in the summer

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.004
in which you said that

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.405
the Biden administration's

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.441
approach to rescuing Americans

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.875
in distress in Iran

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.578
has failed spectacularly so far.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.880
And you've recently gone on a

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.482
I believe, a one week hunger

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.184
strike to draw attention.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.218
Tell me what you mean

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.687
by failed spectacularly so far.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:16.856
I mean,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:17.991
seven and a half years

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:20.960
in, I'm still in Evin Prison.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.628
Look,

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.664
I believe that the U.S.,

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.567
with all its power

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.468
as the

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.936
present superpower in the world,

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.639
has a great amount of leverage

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:35.041
And I believe that had that leverage

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.876
been properly used,

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:39.178
we would have been out a long time ago.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:42.415
I think what is clear

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:44.550
is the folly that the three of us

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.319
and what Morad and I

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.121
are hostages in Iran.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.156
We have not so much as jaywalk.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.292
We've been taken for one reason

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.760
and one reason only,

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.361
and that's because we're U.S.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.496
citizens.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:57.997
And the flip side of

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.266
that is we've only only released

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.469
through a deal with the US

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:04.504
you know,

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:05.171
all they could do

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.573
is repeat that seven and a half years

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.476
this six times the hostage crisis.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.779
What what is it going to take?

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.379
Well, I'm going

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:13.880
to I'm

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.015
going to try to ask you about that.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.583
You know, what is it going to take?

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.284
But first,

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:21.521
you are one of three Americans in Evin.

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:25.525
They are detained on on so-called charges

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.192
of espionage.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:27.393
But you are not

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.162
you are detained and

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.730
sentenced on other charges.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:32.999
Do you have

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:33.633
any a

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:33.966
very I

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:34.834
need to correct you

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.969
that we all have the same charge.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.005
We are all charged under Section

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.306
five of weight

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:42.442
with which is a very nebulous charge

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:44.544
of cooperating

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:46.512
with a hostile state, in our case,

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.447
referring to the

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:49.916
United States of America.

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.218
We cannot first have had access.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.086
I'll just speak

00:05:53.086 --> 00:05:54.187
for myself, though,

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:54.987
that we don't

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.589
we have for ordinary citizens,

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:57.423
we don't have access

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.891
to any classified information

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.393
to give to anyone,

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.562
which is why we were charged

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.230
with Section five or eight

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.698
cooperating with a hostile state.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.500
And I'm very free

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:10.236
to ask details about that.

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:10.870
Yes.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.573
I want to know whether you are

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:15.041
in the same location

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.310
as the other Americans, Mourad Tabar

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:19.812
and Imad Shawki.

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.280
Yes, they currently are.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.249
We haven't always been.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.183
All three of us

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.652
were at the same detention

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.054
center at different times.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:31.858
Obviously, I was taken

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.826
two years

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:36.529
and two and a half years respectively,

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.331
before my heart and mind.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:40.466
But today we're all in the same place.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.835
And do you hope to all

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.871
be released together?

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:45.738
Absolutely.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:46.773
I know what

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.441
it feels like to be left behind,

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:49.675
and I wouldn't

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.577
wish it upon my worst enemy.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.146
We're all in this together,

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.547
and I hope

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:55.982
that this solution

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.451
is found for all of us together.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:06:59.152
Siamak,

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:00.720
we will get your message out

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.788
to the world.

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:03.823
And thank you for being so brave

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.492
as to us to talk to us this time.

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:09.295
I would really appreciate it

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.564
if I can also

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.534
if I could also get a chance

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:17.370
to address the president directly.

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:18.738
Go ahead.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.207
Honestly, I really need

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.508
to be heard of this.

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:25.111
I'm taking this risk

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:26.612
for this opportunity,

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.347
so I hope you give it to me.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:28.881
Go ahead.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:29.949
CMYK

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.251
Look at

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:40.259
President Biden.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:41.994
I certainly here

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.663
and I sincerely appreciate

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:44.664
your administration's

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:45.865
repeated declarations

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:46.499
that freeing the

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:47.533
American hostages in

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:50.837
Iran is its top priority.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.738
But I remain deeply worried

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:53.940
that the White House

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.341
just doesn't appreciate

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:58.077
how dire the situation has become.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:59.946
It's also very hurtful and upsetting

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:01.948
that after 25 months in office,

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.416
you haven't found the time

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:05.518
to meet with our families.

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:08.654
Just to give them some words

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:10.790
of assurance, sir.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:11.691
What I'd imagine

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:12.425
I have now

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.759
collectively languished here

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:16.095
for 18 years,

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:17.096
just

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:18.998
our lives and families

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.566
have been utterly devastated.

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:21.667
We desperately,

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.301
desperately

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:24.270
need you to finally conclude

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.272
that we've suffered long enough.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.206
I said once, hopes

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:34.680
President Biden,

00:08:34.881 --> 00:08:35.481
you and you

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.450
alone have the power to deliver

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.818
on the Obama administration's

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:39.585
broken promise.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:40.653
My firm

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:44.724
I implore you, sir,

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:46.092
to put the lives and liberty

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:47.493
of innocent Americans

00:08:47.493 --> 00:08:50.029
above all the politics involved,

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:50.863
and to just do

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.732
what's necessary to end this nightmare

00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:53.933
and bring us home.

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:54.700
Thank you.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:58.571
We'll get that message out.

00:08:58.571 --> 00:09:00.006
So Mark

00:09:00.473 --> 00:09:03.309
and I hope we can talk again.

00:09:03.576 --> 00:09:04.110
I'm sorry.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.079
I don't be sorry. Okay.

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:10.049
Thank you for doing this.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:11.551
Thank you for doing this.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.318
Thank you.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:15.988
You take care so much about

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:18.691
bye bye bye

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:21.928
So we defy anybody

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:24.897
not to be moved by that cry from prison.

00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:25.631
Of course.

00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:27.066
We reached out to the White House

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:29.035
for comment on this conversation

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:30.002
and they did

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:32.238
give us the following response.

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:33.205
They basically said

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:33.773
Iran's

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:35.207
unjust imprisonment

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:38.144
and exploitation of US citizens for use

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:39.612
as political leverage

00:09:39.612 --> 00:09:41.781
is outrageous, inhumane

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:44.016
and contrary to international norms.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:46.319
The United States will always stand up

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:47.853
for the rights of our citizens

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:50.056
wrongfully detained overseas,

00:09:50.056 --> 00:09:52.391
including Siamak Namazi.

00:09:52.391 --> 00:09:53.492
Senior officials

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:54.727
from both the White House

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:56.362
and the State Department

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:57.663
meet and consult

00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:59.899
regularly with the Namazi family.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.301
And we will continue to do so

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:05.171
until this unacceptable detention ends.

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:08.207
And Siamak is reunited with his family.

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.042
Now, we have also reached out

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:12.078
to the Iranian Foreign Ministry

00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:13.946
about Siamak and his fellow

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.514
American detainees,

00:10:15.514 --> 00:10:17.550
and we're still awaiting their response.

